{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness","id":947546,"title":"Darkly Depraved Disney: The Magic Kingdom in the World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-09T23:01:33-07:00","id":947546,"title":"Darkly Depraved Disney: The Magic Kingdom in the World of Darkness","content":"So, I've always had a soft spot for creepy shit related to disney, and I'm clearly not the only one (given how much creepypasta there is about the parks alone). If Disney exists in ChroD, you've gotta assume that there's Some Shit related to it. Sinister things happening at Disney world fits particularly well into the surreal, paranoid modern horror of Demon and GMC. <br /> <br /> So, who's got ideas? I'll start off with some:<br /> <br /> \u2022 They say no one is ever declared dead on Disney property. What if that's because it's impossible to truly die in a Disney park?<br /> \u2022 The Disney parks would, from a supernatural perspective, be an absolute buffet. A teeming mass of humanity forming a boiling, rich cauldron of passions and emotions. Who takes advantage of this bounty? Or do supernatural creatures find themselves somehow unable to enter or feed at the parks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:44:02-07:00","id":947564,"title":"","content":"Hmm, the first things that come to mind are such things as the Disney parks being Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> What's the ghost of Walt up to? My initial thought would be to have him be consumed by a spirit and have the hybrid entity be the god of disney.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the astral entities based on Disney characters regularly possess the people who dress up as them? <br /> <br /> Do the local changelings have Disney themed courts? Or is Disney a trap designed to make children think that faeries are these great wonderful things, so when a Stranger shows up they willingly go to Arcadia?<br /> <br /> If using the woundgate setting, I wouldn't be surprised if Disney's reach extends into the Shatterlands, or perhaps some Disney employees are illegal aliens of the ultraterrestrial kind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:59:07-07:00","id":947568,"title":"","content":"It's called &quot;The Happiest Place on Earth&quot; for a reason. <i>Something</i> enforces that claim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T04:42:22-07:00","id":947667,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Disney Company&quot; would be a mystery cult, at minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T06:07:11-07:00","id":947710,"title":"","content":"The Haunted Mansion has a problem IRL with people dumping cremated remains secretly during the ride. Real ghosts riding technological ghosts preying on people convinced they aren't real sounds pretty abusable.<br /> <br /> The Shadow landscape probably has a hell of a lot of screechingly ecstatic joy spirits. A thin-skinned mage or out-of-place human seeing those huge open grins racing around, braying laughter, teasing toddlers away from their parents and back to the parade, or cheerfully devouring one another, would probably have an episode. Considering the sheer volume of traffic, I'd imagine Disney has solid, supernaturally practical contingencies in place for those occasional guests who start raving about the Smiley-Faces.<br /> <br /> There is an unthinkably powerful... something, hovering above the spire of Cinderella's Castle, just on the other side of the physical. It looks like a star. It is silent and unapproachable and ineffable. It would be little more than a cosmetic feature, except for the fact that sometimes wishes <i>do </i>come true.<br /> <br /> Also, mascot costumes. I can't think of any clever justifications that aren't hopelessly obvious or derivative, but I'd never forgive myself for passing up easy horror fodder like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 08-10-2016, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:08:52-07:00","id":947741,"title":"","content":"I had a crossover plot concept behind Leviathans trying to take over the parks opposed by Princesses (and optionally Geniuses) that worked as characters. Heading there in November - will have more to comment on afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:03:55-07:00","id":947835,"title":"","content":"I'd rather we kept Princess out of this thread, but you can start your own for that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Walt himself. There's got to be something sinister there, especially the frozen-head thing. I like the idea that, if we're doing this as a crossover thing, pretty much every supernatural society claims that Walt had some connection to them, but the evidence indicates that his deal is way weirder than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:22:48-07:00","id":947851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=947835#post947835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the evidence indicates that his deal is way weirder than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe somebody else got everything that <i>wasn't </i>the head, in exchange? Or is that a little too Headless Body of Agnew?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T11:06:41-07:00","id":947885,"title":"","content":"The Park owners know about the goings-on at the Magic Kingdom. They have people for that. That concession stand owner? That security guard? That ride operator? They're all hunters. The Magic Kingdom has its own dedicated hunter Compact. And they aren't afraid to outsource to supernaturals.<br /> <br /> There's a coterie of vampires who all view the Magic Kingdom as a touchstone; maybe it was the last place they went with their family before they were Embraced, maybe it was just the happiest time of their life, and it lets them hold on to their Humanity. They work the night shift around the park; the owners let them stay because they keep poachers out. They even have the right to feed from a rotating group of the employees; just enough to top them off before they start their shift, and they get breaks to avoid falling into Wassail if they have to exert themselves with a particularly obstinate intruder.<br /> <br /> Some werewolves hang around. They're good for keeping the Joy spirits down, and in return they get to use the loci scattered around the park; they like to hang out in Frontierland and Adventureland.<br /> <br /> A lot of the &quot;performers&quot;? They're actually Changelings. An entire Court operates out of the Magic Kingdom, with the Queen ruling from Cinderella's Castle. It's good to be a member of the Court of Joy in the Happiest Place on Earth\u2122.<br /> <br /> And Mages run around and do what they need to. The Free Council likes hanging out in Tomorrowland, subtly preaching Free Council principles to the Sleepers who visit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 08-12-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T11:23:19-07:00","id":947898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=947851#post947851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe somebody else got everything that <i>wasn't </i>the head, in exchange? Or is that a little too Headless Body of Agnew?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no such thing as &quot;too Headless Body of Agnew&quot;, only &quot;not enough Headless Body of Agnew&quot;.<br /> <br /> And Tomorrowland is totally full of Lemurians. It's probably where the Secret Atomist HQ is. <br /> <br /> I forgot all about the Wyrd. Can you imagine what Disney is like to a changeling? Probably kind of terrifying. Either Disney is in league with the True Fae or they have amazing security measures to keep them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T11:35:08-07:00","id":947905,"title":"","content":"My best formed ideas are for CWOD<br /> <br /> That being said...<br /> <br /> Most likely Vamps have theirs hands in disney world making it harder or easier to get reservations ditto with most other resorts<br /> <br /> I could see a Beast with a Quirky sense of humor, running a ride, or even an entire hotel.<br /> <br /> Or the Princess FanSplat.<br /> <br /> the Hopeful would REALLY thrive in disney world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T12:13:51-07:00","id":947940,"title":"","content":"For Prometheans: the owners have special secret tours for Prometheans who think coming to the Magic Kingdom could give them a breakthrough on the Pilgrimage. They get special handlers escorting them through the park, making sure that Torment or Disquiet never ruin the experience for the Promethean or any other visitors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T12:20:23-07:00","id":947946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=947898#post947898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I forgot all about the Wyrd. Can you imagine what Disney is like to a changeling? Probably kind of terrifying. Either Disney is in league with the True Fae or they have amazing security measures to keep them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah man... you ever ask a folklorist what they think of Disney? Walt was an ally to us, who was trying to weaken the true fae and render them harmless by sanitizing their stories in the human mind, I guess he felt sorry for us. It almost worked too but his death from lung cancer threw all that into chaos that didn't get resolved until 89 when they released the little mermaid. There have been a few ups and downs since then, but the plan IS working trust me, just don't dig too deep into the corporate politics, okay? we lost aren't the only things with a stake in Disney.<br /> <br /> - Daisy Dakota, Fairist Dancer of the Court of Joy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:08:13-07:00","id":947984,"title":"","content":"My only thoughts on this is that Disneyland is prolly devoid of Beasts. Both because inspiring fear is hard as hell on the Happiest Place on Earth and they'd prolly hate being around stories where the monster was humanized or destroyed in the End. For the former, the most popular one is Beast from Beauty and the Beast. <br /> <br /> Now I also imagine two other things. One, I imagine a Beast who takes after the Hunter who killed Bambi's mother. On a more serious notion (or equally serious given how almost everyone hates that hunter, at least anyone who's seen the movie) there was a cancelled Disney Project involving creating a Disney park that was dedicated to the Villains. They would've been known of as &quot;Dark Kingdom&quot;. What if that was created? <br /> <br /> Link for people's reference: <a href=\"http://www.wdwinfo.com/columns/walt-disney-world-never-built.cfm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.wdwinfo.com/columns/walt-...ever-built.cfm</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:32:29-07:00","id":948005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=947984#post947984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only thoughts on this is that Disneyland is prolly devoid of Beasts. Both because inspiring fear is hard as hell on the Happiest Place on Earth and they'd prolly hate being around stories where the monster was humanized or destroyed in the End. For the former, the most popular one is Beast from Beauty and the Beast.<br /> <br /> Now I also imagine two other things. One, I imagine a Beast who takes after the Hunter who killed Bambi's mother. On a more serious notion (or equally serious given how almost everyone hates that hunter, at least anyone who's seen the movie) there was a cancelled Disney Project involving creating a Disney park that was dedicated to the Villains. They would've been known of as &quot;Dark Kingdom&quot;. What if that was created?<br /> <br /> Link for people's reference: <a href=\"http://www.wdwinfo.com/columns/walt-disney-world-never-built.cfm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.wdwinfo.com/columns/walt-...ever-built.cfm</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The whole place would exist simultaneously in the Primordial Dream's Orlando hive and the regular world, with the beasts employees being required to add it as a chamber in their shared lair. Beasts automatically merge with their horrors while in the Dark Kingdom and generally love it because they're BEING PAID TO FEED! Best part is what the Disney corpsec forces do to any heroes that get caught on site. There have been a few guests that turned out to be latent beasts who spontaneously self devoured when they entered the park. These lucky guests are offered free admission for life in exchange for working there in the summers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:38:10-07:00","id":948009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=947984#post947984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only thoughts on this is that Disneyland is prolly devoid of Beasts. Both because inspiring fear is hard as hell on the Happiest Place on Earth and they'd prolly hate being around stories where the monster was humanized or destroyed in the End. For the former, the most popular one is Beast from Beauty and the Beast. </div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree. The Indiana Jones ride scared the living crap out of me when I was a kid. And it is the land of uncanny valley. Plenty of scary stuff for Beasts. Plus, I expect they would take pleasure in showing people how fairy tales REALLY end while there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:47:14-07:00","id":948020,"title":"","content":"Disney has been scaring kids since Snow White. Beasts are fine there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:57:31-07:00","id":948031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=948020#post948020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disney has been scaring kids since Snow White. Beasts are fine there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pinocchio has some seriously dark moments. New Nightmare: You are a Donkey","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:13:44-07:00","id":948050,"title":"","content":"I mean, the entire reason I made this thread was because of all the Disney World creepypastas I've read. <br /> <br /> To me, it goes beyond the individual unintentionally scary elements and into the whole overall thing: the sheer size and power and influence and omnipresence of the Disney corporation just inevitably feels sort of sinister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:00:58-07:00","id":948086,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a Freehold in Orlando who took after the Lands and Main Street and used their power to weave a Bulwark born of Disney Magic.<br /> <br /> I could see at least some of the parks being infiltrated by G-M cultists; it's possible that those accidental deaths that occur are grist for some hidden Infrastructure. <br /> <br /> The Haunted Mansion is actually a powerful source of Plasm for reasons unknown. Ghosts around this part of the park are oddly self-aware, and are bound to unseen Anchors. The park keeps a Krewe on retainer to deal with any &quot;unfortunate incidents&quot;.<br /> <br /> Uncle Walt is secretly still alive, and perhaps the world's most powerful Loyalist Deviant.<br /> <br /> Uncle Walt died, but he was preserved. Then some isiot recently tried to bring him back, and now a Promethean with his face is running around heedless of the consequences.<br /> <br /> I wonder, what is the Hedge and Underworld around Disney like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:04:52-07:00","id":948091,"title":"","content":"Wet, one would assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:04:53-07:00","id":948092,"title":"","content":"According to urban myth, a Cast Member died of a heart attack while loading people onto the D platform at the Tower of Terror once upon a time. His ghost is said to still haunt the attraction, and current Cast Members refuse to ride the D platform alone. They report all sorts of strange occurrences and mechanical problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:14:07-07:00","id":948100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=948091#post948091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wet, one would assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a swamp, but one with bizarre structures and bits of castle masonry seeming to grow around and through the Thorns. The sheer pull the location has in the Wyrd means that the Hedge much more closely matches it than in other places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:18:28-07:00","id":948105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=948092#post948092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to urban myth, a Cast Member died of a heart attack while loading people onto the D platform at the Tower of Terror once upon a time. His ghost is said to still haunt the attraction, and current Cast Members refuse to ride the D platform alone. They report all sorts of strange occurrences and mechanical problems.</div> </div> </div> </div> Speaking of the Tower, <a href=\"http://north-of-reality.tumblr.com/post/148677107960/a-dimension-of-mind\" target=\"_blank\">this treatise</a> seems relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:23:15-07:00","id":948110,"title":"","content":"There's a cell of cast members in the park, the suits don't like them but admit they're useful when the monsters on retainer get too &quot;uppity&quot;. They don't have much in the way of weapons, but their knowledge of the park gives them a plethora of tricks and traps against the monsters. The cell rotates often, but is led by a trio O middle aged cast members who believe it's their duty to protect the people going to the park. It's on the verge of becoming a compact simply because of the sheer size of the park.<br /> <br /> The mascot costumes know who is inside of them. Good cast membes find their days less hot, the families more amicable. The bad ones are roasted after each shift, going to bed each day kicked and bruised from bratty kids. The worst...well, heart attacks do happen.<br /> <br /> The utilidors house a society. Not mutants or undead, but people who believe that Walt will return one day and make their miserable lives mean something for a change. Every few months a cast member or guest is taken, brought to worship at the altar of Micky.<br /> <br /> It's not a joke, Disney has tried to build a president. Only he escaped, and now threatens to actually run for an elected office.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:44:53-07:00","id":948135,"title":"","content":"Cool<br /> <br /> I could see heroes getting inspired in disney world.<br /> <br /> hmmn Any ideas on mages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:52:40-07:00","id":948141,"title":"","content":"Well, I mentioned Lemurians in Epcot. And I figure Paradox is either unusually weak or unusually strong there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:13:46-07:00","id":948159,"title":"","content":"Weak, people think it's all special effects and Imagineering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:21:53-07:00","id":948165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=948159#post948159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weak, people think it's all special effects and Imagineering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that would be the obvious way to do it, but I can't but think it would be fun for it to actually be the opposite, and there's some bizarre magic-dampening field. It would make a fun mystery for the players to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:30:02-07:00","id":948167,"title":"","content":"It's probably a ripe place for werewolves to target. Lots of Essence, lots of spirits, probably an entire hierarchy of greed and money spirits just behind them. It's probably flush with cat shapeshifters and Claimed and beshilu that would make it rough for werewolves. Wouldn't help that the people in charge would be occultists or at least have hired occultists on staff. It would be challenging to keep track of it all, providing the werewolves weren't the ones in charge. Easy to imagine a pack of Bale Hounds behind everything. Hounds of Mammon and Maastraac, Carnala and Baalphegor, Lamashtu and Pseulak. Luring in others with the rich wells of Essence and a seemingly unending amount of worthy prey before they start with the games of corruption.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, my character has ties to Disneyland through his background, spending a lot of time there as a child, well before his First Change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T17:36:36-07:00","id":948194,"title":"","content":"Abandoned by Disney, Abandoned by God.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T17:44:31-07:00","id":948199,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Disney and the CofD, I have a bet going with David Hill and if I win, he has to do a WtA version of the jungle book, but would you guys rather have that or have the 80s dark era expanded to all the other CofD splats, while doing it as a CofD send up of Oliver and company (and the 90s Disney movies), with 80s Trump as the villain connecting the splats. Either way, I am going to try to get him to have send ups of the songs from those movies made and embedded into the PDF so the game master can have a real villain song for the PCs.<br /> <br /> So which one would you guys want?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title"