nger have to devote an expensive amount of resources to finding, training, and paying human performers. Or to create performers whose jobs would require feats unreasonable for human performers. At some point Walt Disney and his Imagineers were successful in creating a real, truly living Animatronic...but as expected from the hazards of Disquiet and Torment, is no longer with them.Maybe the true cause of Walt's death was because of a fatal confrontation with an alive Animatronic in Torment. Since then, the Imagineers, following the parting words of Uncle Walt have tried and failed to recreate the divine miracle of the first Unfleshed. That all of the Audio-Animatronics in the parks know are merely incomplete copies, bereft of the Divine Fire. <br /> <br /> Or maybe not, since there are the many rumors of the Animatronics simply just...getting up to walk around the parks after hours. <br /> <br /> Which likewise fuels rumors that the spurned Unfleshed came back, integrating among the Imagineers, and to this day is attempting to create another member of his kin as another Milestone on his Pilgrimage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:09:00-07:00","id":948495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=948428#post948428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...dammit, I had to find this just before I went to bed.<br /> <br /> Anyways, based on my dive in PtC2:<br /> <br /> It is public knowledge that the Audio-Animatronics were among one of the most technologically advanced pieces of hardware that revolutionized the theme park industry. But the truth behind it being far more what the public knew: that the Disney Company were trying to create artificial performers, what other Created know as the Unfleshed.. So that the Disney company would no longer have to devote an expensive amount of resources to finding, training, and paying human performers. Or to create performers whose jobs would require feats unreasonable for human performers. At some point Walt Disney and his Imagineers were successful in creating a real, truly living Animatronic...but as expected from the hazards of Disquiet and Torment, is no longer with them.Maybe the true cause of Walt's death was because of a fatal confrontation with an alive Animatronic in Torment. Since then, the Imagineers, following the parting words of Uncle Walt have tried and failed to recreate the divine miracle of the first Unfleshed. That all of the Audio-Animatronics in the parks know are merely incomplete copies, bereft of the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> Or maybe not, since there are the many rumors of the Animatronics simply just...getting up to walk around the parks after hours.<br /> <br /> Which likewise fuels rumors that the spurned Unfleshed came back, integrating among the Imagineers, and to this day is attempting to create another member of his kin as another Milestone on his Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soooo....<br /> <br /> That Hopper AA. And the Carnotaurus.<br /> <br /> THANKS FOR THE NIGHTMARE FUEL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T09:39:44-07:00","id":948648,"title":"","content":"The final installment of Abandoned by Disney is probably the most relevant for inspirational purposes. Plus, there's a reference to another Disney creepypasta, The River Country Film, in it. <br /> <br /> That idea about animatronics reminded me of a more recent Disney pasta, called simply &quot;Disney's Animatronics&quot;, which I'd also highly recommend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T11:27:48-07:00","id":948716,"title":"","content":"On an opposite tack:<br /> <br /> There is nothing supernatural about the Magic Kingdom.<br /> <br /> <i>Nothing</i>.<br /> <br /> There are no spirits, no ghosts, and no angels. You'd think there would be Vampires or Changelings chowing down on the crowd, but there aren't. None of the structures are Infrastructure - and you aren't going to find leylines or loci there either.<br /> <br /> There is nothing supernatural about the Magic Kingdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:11:45-07:00","id":948732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=948716#post948716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an opposite tack:<br /> <br /> There is nothing supernatural about the Magic Kingdom.<br /> <br /> <i>Nothing</i>.<br /> <br /> There are no spirits, no ghosts, and no angels. You'd think there would be Vampires or Changelings chowing down on the crowd, but there aren't. None of the structures are Infrastructure - and you aren't going to find leylines or loci there either.<br /> <br /> There is nothing supernatural about the Magic Kingdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psh, please. It's not Denny's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"r