re gods need sacrifice...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T16:51:09-07:00","id":948932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=948756#post948756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've read that one. I wasn't sure, since Geckopirateship referred to something specifically called &amp;quot;Disney's Animatronics&amp;quot;, which is not the same title. Also, &amp;quot;Corruptus&amp;quot; isn't really about AAs. At least not mainly, by my read. It's more about general anomalies and Disney Safety and Security.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://youtu.be/0YxWwZff8Uk\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/0YxWwZff8Uk</a> Here it is. Bizarrely, I can't seem to find it by googling either, I had to look it up on youtube.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T17:45:47-07:00","id":948964,"title":"","content":"Ever since the first roller coasters and haunted house opened, Beasts across the world have realized the potential for amusement and theme parks to serve as fertile feeding grounds.<br /> <br /> Within the more structured realm of theme parks, most Beasts within the industry that if you want to get a good consistent meal, any of the other parks are more suitable grounds then the Disney parks.<br /> <br /> Still, hasn't stopped the Beasts that do choose to work with the Mouse from trying.<br /> <br /> Over the years into both the original Disneyland and the other Disney park's existence, various thrill rides would be added as new attractions. From the Matterhorn Bobsleds as the first steel tube roller coaster, which would later have a new resident in the form of the abominable snowman occupy it...whether that was the form of the Beast that oversaw the attraction or perhaps a Beast that was nostalgic for his Swiss homeland, who knows. Then there's the Twilight Zone Tower of Terror, and how the rides' basic premise provides a built-in cover for dropping unwitting park guests into the Twilight Zone that is a Beast's Lair. Or (at Disneyland) Indiana Jones and the Temple of the Forbidden Eye, that provides a literal mutltitude of Chambers for different kinds of fears (skeletons, bugs, a giant snake) for any Beast. Barring the rumors that the entire attraction is just one Beast's Lair.<br /> <br /> Their biggest achievement being the old Alien Encounter: ExtraTERRORestrial ride. One of the scariest rides in existence and brought in a feast for all the Beasts working at the Magic Kindgom. Evidently, like many other Nightmares, the ride worked TOO well, and it attracted Heroes alike en masse. They were not only successful on getting the ride shut down, but in driving the Begotten associated with the attraction from the Disney company entirely.<br /> <br /> And in its place...well, what many of the Floridian fans considers the most horrifying attraction to ever exist in the park...but for completely different reasons then the previous Alien Encounter.<br /> <br /> (...seriously, this is great. I got more when I get home from work)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T18:16:23-07:00","id":948972,"title":"","content":"While on the subject of rollercoasters, everyone should read Miranda Leek's Twisted. It's the The Room of urban fantasy, and it is glorious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:41:43-07:00","id":949066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=948964#post948964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in its place...well, what many of the Floridian fans considers the most horrifying attraction to ever exist in the park...but for completely different reasons then the previous Alien Encounter.<br /> <br /> (...seriously, this is great. I got more when I get home from work)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the Alien Encounter replaced with a similar attraction with Stitch as the star?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T21:28:13-07:00","id":949098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=949066#post949066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the Alien Encounter replaced with a similar attraction with Stitch as the star?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. However, unlike Alien Encounter, Stitch's Great Escape is meant to be a more comedic attraction over being scary.<br /> <br /> And among theme park fans, it's considered to be the one of the worst attractions in all of Walt Disney World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 08-12-2016, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T22:59:13-07:00","id":949146,"title":"","content":"One of the custodians in the park is a Sin-Eater tasked with dealing with the ghosts that flock to the Magic Kingdom. She's a specialist in the kind of gentle coaxing and &quot;therapy&quot; that' required to deal with the ghost of children that come to the park for solace after their death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:48:18-07:00","id":949283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947546-darkly-depraved-disney-the-magic-kingdom-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=949098#post949098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes. However, unlike Alien Encounter, Stitch's Great Escape is meant to be a more comedic attraction over being scary.<br /> <br /> And among theme park fans, it's considered to be the one of the worst attractions in all of Walt Disney World.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still has that one really cool AA, though. Which is not as cool as Hopper or the Carnotaurus in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T07:04:20-07:00","id":950012,"title":"","content":"It's a Small World (After All) could swing either a classic creepy dolls trope or a comic smashfest . Which segues into, let's say... Ballroom Blitz.<br /> <br /> Also, I just remembered that Gravity Falls is Disney, so you could probably shoehorn some of those moments into some terrifying attractions. Monster Head Island: The Ride? (&quot;<i>Ynitsed Ruoy Retne! Nerdlich Thuom Ym Retne</i>!&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 08-14-2016, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:07:51-07:00","id":950191,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I was talking with a couple of friends on Skype about a topic like this a few months ago! We were toying with a ton of potential ideas for this (some of which were already mentioned here by other people; guess we weren't nearly as original as we thought. -__-'), but we were settling on a Demon game where there was a ton of seemingly abandoned infrastructure scattered around the park (and under it -- the temptation to have some action in the Utilidors is too tempting to pass up!), with the Demons taking the covers of Cast Members in an attempt to claim it for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:32:01-07:00","id":950260,"title":"","content":"The Jungle Cruise is self-sustaining. What was once a collection of plants arranged to create the artificial scenery for a water ride is now a full-fledged ecosystem. At first, landscapers marveled that they needed to spend so little time maintaining it... but eventually, the landscapers began to say that they <i>couldn't </i>maintain it. Plants grew at alarming rates, and eventually animals began to move into the attraction. Eventually, landscapers only pruned and sheered once a year, to keep the jungle from creeping out into the rest of the park. Only a select group of employees are permitted to enter the jungle... and they all sign NDAs upon accepting the job. But there are rumors... usually from former employees who are missing limbs... that something lives in the jungle. And it is <i>hungry. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T00:27:50-07:00","id":950464,"title":"","content":"There have been these weird spirits, hybrid spirits of anger and despair... some of them seem to have traits from vehicle spirits, or nature spirits, or animal spirits... They only seem to apear in the Shadow or the Twilight around Disney Parks, but they don't seem to be feeding on anything present... The weird thing is that not one such spirit existed prior to March 28, 2002. Something happened that day to bring them into existance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 08-14-2016, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","nam