er":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:36:34-07:00","id":951281,"title":"","content":"Whose Line was supposed to run as long as all the performers were alive. So who brought them all back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T16:18:03-08:00","id":1054496,"title":"","content":"So...clearing out my work computer, found a text file of a post for this thread, but forgot about until now. Finished up the post, and here we are.<br /> <br /> <b>Museum of the Weird</b><br /> <br /> <br /> In the years when the Haunted Mansion was being created by the Imagineers, there were plans to make a companion attraction to the Haunted Mansion. Dubbed &quot;The Museum of the Weird&quot; it was a walk through attraction through a museum that was the home of many strange and unusual artifacts that the Disney Company collected all over the world. Some of which we now via the concept art that came out in the years since:<br /> <br /> the Melting Candle Man<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://waltdisney.org/sites/default/files/hauntedmansion_candleman.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> the Coffin Clock<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.betterhaunts.com/weirdclock.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> and the Mistress of Evil.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/8b/e9/04/8be9048033c7eedc9e58cc7c210a2534.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> There have even been additional writings about a Giraffe Piano and the Mothman (yes, perhaps THAT Mothman).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the attraction never made it out of the pre-production stage due to Walt's death and the upheaval in the company caused many projects to either be canceled, shelved, or heavily downsized. The Museum of the Weird was, unfortunately, one of those canceled projects being the Museum of the Weird.<br /> <br /> The Imagineers, however, have a hard time letting anything go. Especially good ideas.<br /> <br /> Some of those ideas include the Chair with a Face or some of the designs.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.doombuggies.com/images/history_crump_chairs.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> But where things get interesting is what happens after the Mansion opens.<br /> <br /> Various supernaturals (be they Spirit Mages, a Bone Shadow of a Forsaken pack, or a Krewe of Sin Eaters) have confirmed that there is some ghost and spirit activity that circles around the Chair with the Face. And further scrutiny suggests that this Chair has had these properties since it was first made, and as long as that chair has been in the Mansion.<br /> <br /> Years later another one of the artifacts popped up in an auction: the Reaper Clock.<br /> <br /> While the various Floridian supernaturals have a multitude of theories on the existence of the Museum of the Weird items.<br /> <br /> 1. The original premise of the attraction is actually 100% true and the Disney Company really did acquire occult items all across the world and wanted to put them on display in a Disney attraction.<br /> <br /> They could be Urathra Fetishes, Supernal Artifacts, Athanors, Relics, or any other possible supernatural item.<br /> <br /> 2. The Disney Company crafted all of the items themselves to be put up on display as an attraction.<br /> <br /> Of course that just leaves the question of: what happened to the rest of the items?<br /> <br /> Were they destroyed when plans of the attraction fell through? Or were they simply...stored away somewhere? Either way, any of the various supernatural societies would eagerly await any information about the other items for study and to perhaps use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:37:10-08:00","id":1054595,"title":"","content":"If only you could see the tunnels underneath Magic Kingdom. There are many things down there that cannot be explained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T23:01:22-08:00","id":1054664,"title":"","content":"The Yippie Invasion of Disney Land back in the 70s was used as a cover for various operations by supernatural factions in the